9]]}, {"t": " no", "lp": -1.082362413406372, "top": [[" no", -1.082362413406372], [" **", -1.2700283527374268]]}, {"t": " c", "lp": -0.4923277795314789, "top": [[" c", -0.4923277795314789], [" compiler", -1.2183924913406372]]}, {"t": "cache", "lp": -0.0015428040642291307, "top": [["cache", -0.0015428040642291307], ["make", -7.651017189025879]]}, {"t": "/", "lp": -0.8741938471794128, "top": [["/", -0.8741938471794128], [" (", -1.3442256450653076]]}, {"t": "comp", "lp": -1.4902163743972778, "top": [["comp", -1.4902163743972778], ["ice", -1.9791052341461182]]}, {"t": "ilation", "lp": -1.050065040588379, "top": [["ilation", -1.050065040588379], ["il", -1.298497200012207]]}, {"t": " database", "lp": -1.2567967176437378, "top": [[" database", -1.2567967176437378], [" cache", -1.6369503736495972]]}], "text": "# PKGBUILD build() Function: Step-by-Step Explanation\n\nLet me break down this `build()` function line by line.\n\n## The Setup\n\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\n```\nThis loads the Intel oneAPI environment variables (compiler paths, library paths, etc.). The `--force` flag forces the environment to be set up even if it appears already configured. This is essential because we're compiling with Intel's SYCL toolchain (`icx`/`icpx`).\n\n```bash\nset -e\n```\nThis makes the script exit immediately if any command returns a non-zero status (an error). A safety net so a failed compile stops the build rather than continuing.\n\n## The CMake Invocation\n\n```bash\ncmake -S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\" -B \"${srcdir}/build\" -G Ninja\n```\n- `-S`: **S**ource directory (where the source code lives)\n- `-B`: **B**uild directory (where build artifacts go)\n- `-G Ninja`: Use the **Ninja** build generator (fast, minimal-output build system)\n\n## CMake Configuration Flags\n\n| Flag | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| `-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release` | Optimize for performance (enables `-O3`, strips debug info) |\n| `-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr` | Where files install (root filesystem) |\n| `-DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib` | Libraries go in `/usr/lib` |\n| `-DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=icx` | Use Intel C compiler |\n| `-DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=icpx` | Use Intel C++ compiler |\n| `-DCMAKE_C_COMPILER_LAUNCHER=` | Empty \u2192 no ccache/compilation database"}